  "about": "ScreenInputOrigin (Sources/ScreenControlCore/ScreenInputOrigin.swift), DESIGN docs/design/mac-to-mac-2026-11-01 SR-26, SR-29, S-M3. InputOriginChecks.swift runs every vector; tests/screen-input-origin-sync.test.ts holds `rules` equal to the Control bar (native/computer-use ComputerUseControlCore/ControlBarRules.swift) and to the Swift constants. expect is \"accept\" or a ScreenInputRefusal code.",
  "fields": "keyboardType and sourceState are illustrative until S-M3 records measured values (sourceState 1 = kCGEventSourceStateHIDSystemState). Under the unmeasured calibration only sourcePid decides; InputOriginChecks varies both fields to prove it. sourcePid is an S-M3 premise too (DESIGN 13절): these vectors take only the HID system to post as pid 0, and every other program, remote desktops included, to carry its own pid. A vector whose verdict rests on an unmeasured premise names it in premise (virtual-hid-pid-0: a virtual HID device; synthetic-pid-0: a program that writes 0 into eventSourceUnixProcessID before posting; remote-desktop-pid-0: Jump or Apple screen sharing input that arrives without its own pid) with measured false, and one that expects accept carries a residualRisk that starts with the premise. Recording S-M3 rewrites each: refused and measured when the calibration tells the source apart, accepted and measured with its residualRisk when it cannot, removed when the source never reads as pid 0.",
